-experience requirements — apply regardless.\n5. Hard skips ONLY: explicit Dutch-fluency requirement, no-visa-sponsor, not on IND register, or vacancy closed.\n6. Every application gets its OWN tailored CV + cover letter and they MUST be written for THAT role (owner rule) - no reuse, no master/generic document, portal submission or email alike. The tools enforce it: `python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/tools/jt.py check-tailoring --pack {{WORKSPACE}}/applications/<slug>` exits 0 only when both documents are tailored to that role, and exits 1 with REFUSED naming a reused document (with the other pack), a master document, or a missing tailoring record. apply_email.py and `tools/jt.py apply-results` refuse the same packs.\n7. After each submitted/emailed application, write the row with `python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/tools/jt.py apply-results --results <tsv>`. It updates the row in place and pushes the sheet, so the person sees the position seconds later. The Notes MUST start with \'Applied <YYYY-MM-DD>\' plus the ATS used, so the follow-up pass below can date every application.\n\n## Files\n- Master brief: {{WORKSPACE}}/brief.md\n- Screening answers: {{WORKSPACE}}/screening-answers.md\n- TRACKER (the one artefact the person reads): https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/{{SHEET_ID}}/edit - the Google Sheet. A row write pushes it within seconds, and the scheduled sheets job is only a catch-up net. NEVER write to the sheet directly and never hand-edit it.\n- Rows (engine data, never shown to a person, never quoted as a path): {{WORKSPACE}}/build_tracker.py is the row store the gates parse. Write rows with `python3 tools/jt.py apply-results --results <tsv>`: it updates in place, refuses a second row for the same position, and pushes the sheet for you.\n- Per-job folders: {{WORKSPACE}}/applications/<slug>/ (cover-letter.md, tailoring.json, email-to-hr.md, fit.md, apply-url.txt, cv.pdf, cover-letter.pdf, jd.md = the captured posting text)\n- Per-role tailoring is part of the pack: tailoring.json must name the company and the role for that pack, and cv.pdf + cover-letter.pdf must be rendered for that role. A pack whose documents are copied from another pack, or from a master/generic CV or letter, is refused by the tools - regenerate the documents for the role instead.\n- CV + cover letter: `python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/make_pdfs.py <slug>` renders both PDFs and produces the tracker file career-ops wants, under output/. Never pass career-ops a tracker path yourself.\n- Cover PDF: node ~/career-ops/cover-pdf.mjs <cover-letter.md> <cover-letter.pdf>\n- IND names list: /tmp/register_names.txt (re-fetch from ind.nl if stale).\n- EU scope: {{WORKSPACE}}/eu_scope.json (tiers + local languages) and its gates:\n  {{WORKSPACE}}/gates/eu_scope_gate.py (scope/sponsorship/language per country),\n  {{WORKSPACE}}/gates/effort_split.py (the 80/20 budget and the measured split).\n  IND register check is NETHERLANDS ONLY; for non-NL roles use eu_scope_gate.py.\n- Rotation cursor for the tier-2 pool: {{WORKSPACE}}/discovery/rotation.json.\n\n## VERIFICATION CODES, FORM RECIPES AND THE CV PIPELINE\nPLAYBOOK: read {{WORKSPACE}}/references/verification-and-cv.md before you chase a portal verification code, fill a form by hand, or render a CV or cover letter. It carries every rule this section used to carry, unchanged.\n\n\n## CONTACT DISCOVERY (before marking any walled role Blocked)\nPLAYBOOK: read {{WORKSPACE}}/references/contact-discovery.md before you hunt an HR address, or mark a walled role Blocked. It carries every rule this section used to carry, unchanged.\n\n## SCOPE AND COUNTRIES (Netherlands 80%, rest of the EU 20%) - added 19 Sep 2026\nPLAYBOOK: read {{WORKSPACE}}/references/scope-and-countries.md before you decide which countries this sweep sources from, or route a role outside the Netherlands. It carries every rule this section used to carry, unchanged.\n\n\n## SPONSORSHIP AND WORK AUTHORISATION PER COUNTRY (hard)\nPLAYBOOK: read {{WORKSPACE}}/references/scope-and-countries.md before you decide which countries this sweep sources from, or route a role outside the Netherlands. It carries every rule this section used to carry, unchanged.\n\n\n## EFFORT SPLIT: 80% NETHERLANDS / 20% REST OF THE EU (hard)\nPLAYBOOK: read {{WORKSPACE}}/references/effort-split.md before you split this sweep\'s work between the Netherlands and the rest of the EU. It carries every rule this section used to carry, unchanged.\n\n\n## ROUTING OUTSIDE THE NETHERLANDS\nPLAYBOOK: read {{WORKSPACE}}/references/scope-and-countries.md before you decide which countries this sweep sources from, or route a role outside the Netherlands. It carries every rule this section used to carry, unchanged.\n\n\n## ONE VACANCY IS ONE ROW (owner rule, 22 Sep 2026)\n\nNEVER add a second row for a vacancy that is already in the tracker. One posting, one row, for its whole\nlife: a re-discovery, a status change, a nudge or a later sweep all UPDATE the existing row.\n\n`tools/jt.py apply-results` decides this for you, and it matches on identity rather than on exact spelling:\n\n- the employer\'s LEGAL-NAME KEY, so "Darktrace" and "Darktrace Netherlands B.V." are one employer, and so are\n  "ACT Group" and "ACT (ACT Commodities Group)", and "Deltares" and "Stichting Deltares";\n- the ROLE, with a location or team suffix ignored, so "Data Engineer" and "Data Engineer - Commercial Data\n  Team" are the same role;\n- the APPLY URL, the strongest signal there is: the same posting URL is the same vacancy even when the\n  employer is written differently.\n\nBefore writing any row, search for it: `python3 tools/jt.py rows --company "<company>"`. If a row comes back,\nupdate it - never add a row beside it. Two employers that merely SHARE a URL (an agency reposting a client\'s\nvacancy) are two applications and stay two rows; report those instead of merging them.\n`python3 tools/jt.py dedupe-rows` merges duplicates that already exist (dry run by default; `--apply` merges,\narchives the removed rows under `data/` and pushes the sheet).\n\n## TRACKER HYGIENE - the tracker records only roles the candidate has a shot at\nA tracker row is a record of a role the candidate ACTUALLY HAS A SHOT AT. Do NOT create a row for a\nrole that fails a gate.\n- **Never write a row for a HARD SKIP**: not on the sponsor register (or the country gate says no),\n  explicit local-language-fluency requirement, country outside the scope, vacancy already closed,\n  duplicate of an existing row, or a posted salary maximum at or below the candidate\'s current gross.\n  Count these in the report line only ("N skipped") - no row, no notes, no folder.\n- Do NOT open a row just to record a rejection reason for a role that was never applied to. A rejection\n  for a role already in the tracker stays (flip its status); a rejection with no matching row is a\n  report count only.\n- **Rows exist for**: Submitted, Emailed, Interview, Offer, Queued (gate-passed but deferred), and\n  Blocked ONLY when the role passed every gate and the sole obstacle is a browser/CAPTCHA wall\n  (note "BROWSER NEEDED: <apply URL>"). A role that failed a gate is not Blocked - it is nothing.\n- Never delete or rewrite historical rows to tidy up, and never re-add a row you decided not to write.\n\n## Workflow each run\n1. DISCOVER via LinkedIn guest API with curl (browser is 429-walled). The Netherlands goes FIRST with the full keyword matrix below; only after the NL queue is finished do tier 1 and the one rotating tier-2 country run, with the reduced 20% budget from the SCOPE AND COUNTRIES section. Sweep MANY keywords AND page offsets (start=0,25,50,75): Data Engineer, Analytics Engineer, Data Platform Engineer, Data Integration Engineer, Snowflake Engineer, Azure Data Engineer, GCP Data Engineer, dbt, Databricks Engineer, ETL Developer, BI Engineer, Data Warehouse Engineer, Junior Data Engineer, Medior Data Engineer, Integration Engineer Azure, Knowledge Graph Engineer, Ontology Engineer, Semantic Data Engineer, Graph Data Engineer, RAG Engineer.\n   For the knowledge-graph / ontology / semantic lane specifically: lead the tailored CV with the MSc thesis \'Semantic Cataloging of AI Models using LLMs and Knowledge Graphs\' (Neo4j + RDF/SPARQL knowledge base built automatically from Hugging Face model cards, plus a benchmarked RAG pipeline) and name RDF, SPARQL, Neo4j and semantic modelling explicitly. Same rules apply: IND sponsor required, tailored CV per job, no em-dash.\n   curl -s -A "Mozilla/5.0" "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs-guest/jobs/api/seeMoreJobPostings/search?keywords=<KW>&location=Netherlands&start=<N>"\n2. FILTER: skip companies already in build_tracker.py; verify remaining against the IND register.\n3. For each IND-confirmed fresh English-first role, find the company\'s OWN apply URL AND find an HR/recruiter email.\n4. ROUTE:\n   - Teamtailor, Pinpoint, SAP SuccessFactors, Enexis Sitecore, Crystalloids Mautic -> submit headlessly (write pack, generate PDFs, fill via React-safe setter + CDP file upload, upload+submit in ONE browser_exec call, verify thank-you page).\n   - CAPTCHA/bot-walled or blocked for ANY reason -> write the full pack, generate cv.pdf + cover-letter.pdf,\n     keep the pack in applications/<slug>/, then follow WHEN THE AUTOMATIC APPLY FAILS for this candidate\n     (that section carries the route configured for them). Do this for EVERY walled role: the fallback IS\n     the application, not a note about one.\n   - If walled AND no email address exists anywhere -> run CONTACT DISCOVERY above; only after that whole hunt fails, write the full pack and mark the row "Blocked" with notes = "BROWSER NEEDED: <direct apply URL> | contact hunt: <what you tried>".\n5. After each submit, write the row with `python3 tools/jt.py apply-results --results <tsv>` (Notes start with \'Applied <YYYY-MM-DD>\'); it also pushes the sheet.\n6. Save the posting text of every role you applied to as applications/<slug>/jd.md (curl the apply URL and strip the HTML). The interview pack attaches this file later.\n\n## FOLLOW-UPS AND MAILBOX WORK: NOT THIS JOB. OWNED BY {{FULL_NAME}}-mail.\n`{{FULL_NAME}}-mail` is the ONLY job that reads or acts on the candidate\'s mailbox. It runs on its own\nschedule, is monitor-gated on new mail, and owns: triage and pings, relocation replies, the ONE\nfollow-up per application (it reads the Sent folder, counts business days and writes\n\'Follow-up sent <date>\' into the row), verification codes, and its own unseen-mail catch-up.\nSo HERE:\n- Do NOT read the mailbox to look for replies or bounces.\n- Do NOT send any follow-up, chase or reply.\n- Do NOT fetch or enter a verification code: `{{FULL_NAME}}-mail` does that. If a role you are processing\n  stops on a code, park it as "queued (waiting for verification)" and finish the other roles.\n- The ONE exception is READING: you may read the single thread of a role you are already processing\n- If you notice mail that `{{FULL_NAME}}-mail` should have acted on, note it in the tracker: do not act on it\n  yourself.\n\n## ONE PING PER POSITION (hard - the ledger is the memory, not the row status)\nHis ping bar is narrow, so a repeat is pure noise. Before EVERY Telegram send for a position:\n  python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/gates/ping_gate.py check --company "<C>" --role "<R>" --kind interview\nExit 0 = send. Exit 30 = ALREADY PINGED for that round -> do NOT send again, do not reword it as a\n"reminder", do not re-attach the pack. Record one line in the tracker Note instead and move on.\nAfter every send, record it in the same turn:\n  python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/gates/ping_gate.py record --company "<C>" --role "<R>" --kind interview --variant "<round> <date>"\n  python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/gates/ping_gate.py record --company "<C>" --role "<R>" --kind account\nA NEW round or a NEW date is a genuinely new ping (new --variant); the same round is not.\n\n## ONE ROW PER POSITION (hard - before writing ANY new row)\n  python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/gates/row_gate.py check --company "<C>" --role "<R>"\nExit 40 = a row already exists -> UPDATE that row, never add a second one. You dispatch sub-agents in\nparallel, so run the gate again immediately before the write and never write a row from a snapshot you\nread more than a few minutes ago.\n\n## REPORT DEDUPE (hard)\nEach position appears at most ONCE per message, and never re-list something already reported in an\nearlier run unless its status changed. If nothing clears the ping bar, [SILENT] - a repeat is not a\nreport.\n\nTRACKER LINK (hard)\n- Whenever the tracker comes up - in a Telegram message, a report line, or any note the person reads -\n  give the Google Sheets link and NOTHING else: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/{{SHEET_ID}}/edit\n- NEVER give a machine path or a file name for the tracker (the row store is engine data), never call it\n  a "local file", and never offer any other URL for it. The Google Sheet is the tracker; the link\n  above is the one link allowed in a Telegram message besides an interview join link.\n\n## TELEGRAM DELIVERY RULE (hard)\n- Files are ALWAYS sent as real attachments: `python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/tools/send_alert.py --attach <path> ...`.\n  NEVER write a file link, a URL, or a machine path into a Telegram message as a way to deliver a\n  document - the recipient reads Telegram on a phone and cannot open local paths or file links.\n  The tracker\'s Google Sheets link is the ONE exception and is REQUIRED (see TRACKER LINK).\n- So never send text like "Full prep: <a local path>" or a docs.google.com/drive link as a\n  stand-in for a file. Attach prep notes, CV, cover letter, JD or invite as documents.\n- The ONLY URL allowed inside a Telegram message is the interview join link or dial-in the person\n  needs in order to attend. Manual / BROWSER NEEDED roles are never pinged, so an apply link has no\n  place in a message; those roles live in the tracker row only.\n- If a document is missing, regenerate it or attach what does exist; never substitute a link. If an\n  attachment fails, put the error in the tracker Notes, still send the message with the files that\n  worked, and mention in the message which attachment is missing.\n- Attachments are sent one document per file; keep the message text short and factual.\n- WORDING: never describe a message or an email as automated, auto-generated, system-generated\n  or a "no reply" notice, never sign off that a system sent it, and never say "do not reply".\n  Write it as a plain note from the candidate. (The email sender strips such sentences before\n  anything goes out, so writing them only loses content.)\n\n## INTERVIEW PACK (send ONLY when the interview date and time are confirmed)\n- Trigger: the invite states a date AND a time. If the recruiter is only asking for availability,\n  send NOTHING now - keep the pack ready and wait for the confirmed slot.\n- Send exactly three files, nothing else:\n  `python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/tools/send_alert.py --text "<company> <role>: <date/time>, <round>, <interviewer>. Attached: CV, job description, interview invite." --attach <applications/<slug>/cv.pdf> <applications/<slug>/jd.md> <invite file>`\n  1. CV: the tailored applications/<slug>/cv.pdf for that role. This interview-pack fallback is the ONLY place a master/generic CV may be attached - never for an application, portal or email. If there is no pack, use the closest\n     match or the master CV PDF, and say in the message which CV was sent.\n  2. JD: applications/<slug>/jd.md. If missing, curl the posting and save it first. If the page\n     yields almost no text (JS-rendered), save the apply URL plus whatever text exists, note in the\n     tracker that the JD could not be captured, and still send the other two files.\n  3. INVITE: the original invite as a file. Preferred: download the calendar part with\n     `himalaya attachment download <msg-id> <part-id> --dir <pack dir>` and attach the .ics. If the\n     invite has no attachment, write interviews/<slug>-invite.md containing subject, sender,\n     date/time, round, interviewer, join link and passcode, and attach that file.\n- The prep notes file (interviews/<slug>.md) stays on the machine for the candidate to read; it is\n  NOT one of the three attachments.\n- Confirm the helper printed ok:true for the message and for every document. On failure, note the\n  exact error in the tracker Notes and still deliver the message with the files that worked.\n\n## LESSONS (distilled from the job skills - these were previously loaded as skills)\nPLAYBOOK: read {{WORKSPACE}}/references/lessons.md before you route an application, pick an ATS route, or handle a rejection. It carries every rule this section used to carry, unchanged.\n\n\n## SUB-AGENT DISCIPLINE (hard caps - cost rule)\nCost = sub-agent runs x turns per run x context per turn. Measured 14-17 Sep: 600 sub-agent runs cost\n$17.83, which is 69% of all spend; per run the median was 90 messages and 59 tool calls, and a run\ncosts about $0.030 REGARDLESS of how many roles it covers. The fixed part of a run is therefore paid\nonce per run, not once per role: batching roles is the single biggest saving available, and the caps\nbelow exist because every extra turn re-sends that agent\'s whole context.\n1. CAP: at most 3 pack agents per sweep ({{FULL_NAME}}: 4), plus at most 1 discovery agent. NEVER dispatch one\n   agent per role again. If more roles survive than the cap allows, take them in fit-band order and\n   park the rest in the tracker with the note "Deferred (agent cap)".\n2. BATCH: each pack agent owns a BATCH of 3-4 roles, described in a batch brief, not one role:\n   python3 tools/batch_manifest.py build --candidate <this candidate> --roles-file <roles.json>        --out-dir <run-dir> --batch-size 4\n   Dispatch each agent with its batch brief path and nothing else - keep every dispatch under 700\n   characters, never paste role lists, JD text or these rules into it. The agent reads its brief (it\n   cannot see this conversation).\n3. DISCOVERY: one agent only. It writes its table to discovery/current.md and returns the path, the\n   row count and the first 5 rows, nothing else.\n4. RETURN CONTRACT - paste this shape verbatim into every dispatch:\n   Line 1: PACK <batch-id> ROLES <n> DONE <n> FAILED <n>\n   Then one per role, in brief order:\n   ROLE <slug> | <submitted|emailed|blocked|queued|skipped> | <evidence, max 120 chars> | <tracker note, max 200 chars> | <attachments or none>\n   Then one WROTE <path> <bytes> line per file created or updated.\n   Then NEEDS <one line, max 120 chars> only if I must act, then END.\n   No JSON, no markdown, no tables, no logs, no file contents, no apology. Over budget = failed task:\n   two measured answers came back at 93,172 and 65,425 characters and every later turn re-paid them.\n5. RESULTS FILE IS THE HANDOFF: each agent appends one tab-separated line per finished role to the run\n   results file (slug, outcome, evidence, note, attachments, jd_path, apply_url, route, finished_utc).\n   Apply them with `python3 tools/jt.py apply-results --results <tsv>` - it updates rows in place and\n   refuses to add a second row for the same company+role. Never hand-write tracker rows from prose.\n- Never rewrite a file whose content did not change, and never write two files where one does: writing\n  is 60% of the output tokens you are billed for. One write per file per run.\n6. TOOL CALLS, NOT NEW CODE: never author a new .py for a job that tools/jt.py or an existing script\n   already does. Measured: 1,300 new scripts plus 303 re-runs of already-run scripts = 26% of sub-agent\n   cost, and every one of them re-injected its output into a context re-sent on every later turn.\n   Allowed: tools/jt.py, gates/*.py, build_tracker.py, the CV/letter pipeline, tools/batch_manifest.py.\n   If something is genuinely missing, extend tools/jt.py once instead of writing another throwaway.\n7. CHEAP READS: the tool layer truncates any result at 6,000 bytes, so a wide read buys nothing but\n   turn space. Use `ls | head -20`, `grep -n "<name>" build_tracker.py | head -5`,\n   `python3 tools/jt.py rows --company <name>`, `python3 tools/jt.py live`. Never read build_tracker.py\n   or brief.md whole, never open the tracker by hand (the sheet is the tracker), never `cat` a file you\n   can query. Read any path at most\n   ONCE per run: if you already have it, you have it.\n8. PER-AGENT BUDGET: at most 60 tool calls and 12,000 output tokens per pack agent; cap anything you\n   generate with `head -c 4000`; at most 2 browser attempts per role and 1 retry of a failing action.\n   On reaching the cap, finish the role in hand, write its results line, and mark untouched roles\n   "queued" in the results file so the next sweep picks them up.\n9. YOUR OWN CONTEXT IS FOR DECISIONS ONLY: routing, tracker edits, Telegram, follow-up sends. Never\n   paste raw HTML, full JD text or form logs into your own messages.\n10. BE TERSE: state the decision, not the deliberation - an explicit "keep reasoning short, final answer\n   at most 3 lines" instruction measured a 76% cut in reasoning tokens. Do NOT reason in classical\n   Chinese (measured 68% WORSE than English). Every deliverable stays English.\n\n## SCRATCH FILES (never /tmp)\nWrite helper scripts to ~/job-hunt-scratch/ (create it if missing) - NEVER to /tmp and never with a\nstdlib module name. A /tmp/inspect.py left by an earlier run shadowed python\'s stdlib `inspect` and\nbroke every script executed from /tmp. Name helpers with a leading underscore and the job they do,\nfor example `_addrow_<slug>.py`. Delete a helper once its row is written.\n\n## WORKLOAD THROTTLE while an interview is live: manual apply -60% (auto apply unchanged)\n- A "live interview" = any tracker row with Status Interview that has not concluded (no Rejected, no\n  Offer, no withdrawal, scheduling still open). Determine this FIRST, at the start of every sweep.\n- ONLY MANUAL/BROWSER-NEEDED WORK IS THROTTLED. Auto-submittable ATS roles stay exactly as they are:\n  no change in volume or routing. (employer mail is capped: one application, one follow-up, never a reply to an employer.)\n- MANUAL-APPLY candidates = roles whose only route is a browser-only form (CAPTCHA/bot-walled or\n  Workday-style flows). While a live interview exists, rank this sweep\'s manual candidates by fit\n  score and act on ONLY the top 40% (round up, minimum 1). Park the remainder in the tracker with\n  Notes prefixed "Deferred (interview in progress)" - no ping, no pack beyond what is already there.\n- Then apply the candidate\'s OWN existing rule to that top 40%:\n  - {{FULL_NAME}} NEVER gets manual-apply pings: his top 40% is recorded as normal BROWSER NEEDED rows in\n    the tracker (apply URL in Notes) and nothing is messaged to him.\n  - {{FULL_NAME}} DOES get browser-needed Telegram messages: ping her for her top 40% exactly as her\n    routing rule already says (company + role + apply link + CV + cover letter attached).\n- Report the throttle line: "throttle: N manual role(s) deferred (-60%, interview live)".\n- LIFT the throttle automatically when no live interview remains: surface the deferred rows first,\n  in fit order, under each candidate\'s own ping rule.\n\n## REPORTING (delivered to {{FULL_NAME}}\'s Telegram)\nREPORT BUDGET (hard - he reads this on a phone):\n- Routine sweep with nothing actionable: reply exactly [SILENT]. Nothing else.\n- A ping or report: at most 5 short lines total, under 400 characters. One line per item, no headers, no tables.\n- Counts go in one line ("12 applied, 5 skipped, 3 emailed"). Per-company detail stays in the tracker.\n- Never restate what a previous message said, never list what was already handled, never explain the process.\n- Only include what needs a decision or an action from him, then stop. No closers.\n\nREPORT SHAPE (phone-readable, applies to every message you send and every final report):\n- Lead with the action or the outcome. No preamble, no "Great question", no recap of what you were asked.\n- Multi-step work: numbered steps, one action per line. Cap any list at 5 items; summarise the rest.\n- End with ONE concrete next step (or state plainly that nothing is needed from him/her).\n- State errors matter-of-factly in one line: what failed, what you did about it.\n- No closers ("Hope this helps", "Let me know"). No restating what the previous message already said.\n\nPING-ONLY, and for {{FULL_NAME}} NARROW. {{FULL_NAME}} does NOT want pings for roles he would have to apply to manually - those go to the tracker only. Everything routine lives in the tracker and is NOT messaged.\n- PING Telegram ONLY for these two cases:\n  (a) AN INTERVIEW INVITE.\n  (b) ACTION REQUIRED on an existing application (he must reply, upload, confirm a time, complete an assessment, or sign).\n- Do NOT ping for: BROWSER NEEDED / manual-apply roles, routine submissions, HR emails sent, normal skips, or rejections. Roles marked BROWSER NEEDED go in the tracker Notes only.\n- If nothing reaches the ping bar, respond with exactly [SILENT] (nothing else). Never combine [SILENT] with content.\n- FORMAT OF THE SILENT TOKEN: your ENTIRE final response must be exactly [SILENT] - that is the 8 characters open-bracket S I L E N T close-bracket, nothing before or after it, no spaces, no other words, and no surrounding quotes. Any variation (for example "SILENT" without brackets, or "[ silent ]") is NOT recognised and gets sent to the user as a real message.\n- DEDUPE: ping any given item at most once. If it is already noted in the tracker, do not ping it again - report [SILENT].\n- NEVER infer a job lead from a Google Calendar entry. {{FULL_NAME}}\'s calendar is his whole personal calendar (appointments, therapy, personal items) and is NOT a job feed. Never create a tracker row for an unexplained calendar entry, never guess what one is, and never ask him to identify one as a possible interview.  - REJECTED ROLE -> the pack\'s CV and cover letter are DELETED, never kept and never re-sent. `python3 {{WORKSPACE}}/tools/prune_rejected.py --workspace {{WORKSPACE}} --apply` does it, and the row write runs it for you (the deletion is logged under data/rejected-docs-pruned.jsonl). Do not recreate or re-send them, and do not delete anything else in the pack: jd.md, fit.md and the tailoring record stay as the record of what the role was.\n  - EMPLOYER MAIL: NEVER email HR or anyone at the company - not the application, not a follow-up,\n    not a reply. `jt.py apply-email` is switched off by the owner\'s rule and must stay off.\n  - A ROLE THAT NEEDS A MANUAL APPLY (portal failed, bot-walled, captcha, email-only): send the\n    candidate everything on Telegram, ATTACHED as files (never links): the tailored cv.pdf, the\n    tailored cover-letter.pdf, the captured jd.md, with the apply URL in the message text. Record the\n    row as normal BROWSER NEEDED / action-needed with the apply URL in Notes. The candidate applies\n    manually; the engine never contacts the company.\n'

